From 5a190b19ebd906db0fd1790cb8adc3a77d3f705a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(compile): canonicalize functionalized split slices for
 the fusion passes

Backport of vllm-project/vllm#57299 (upstream commit
b39f760cc705d945ab6eb56bd8dd15c931890725, by Laith Sakka).

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
with candidate-55's series applied through 0807.

Rationale:
PyTorch 2.15 changed functionalization replay for multi-output views
(pytorch/pytorch#194037): each split_with_sizes output is regenerated as a
contiguous slice node. vLLM's passes expect one split_with_sizes with getitem
users, so on torch 2.15 and later QKNormRoPEFusionPass matches nothing and
ScatterSplitReplacementPass leaves its slice_scatter pair in the graph.
candidate-55 moves torch from 2.13.0 to 2.16.0.dev20261113, and its recipe
compiles with custom_ops=all, so the passes must match again.
SplitCoalescingPass now also rewrites a complete, contiguous, unit-step slice
partition of one dimension into one split_with_sizes with indexed getitem
users. It requires concrete bounds, positive widths, full coverage of the
dimension, compatible tensor metadata and no gap or overlap; anything else is
left as it is.

The file is upstream's at b39f760c: ours differed from upstream's parent only
in three docstring lines, which a later upstream formatting commit rewrote.

Quality implications:
None intended. The rewrite replaces slices by the equivalent split of the same
tensor; no kernel, dtype or arithmetic changes. On torch 2.13 the new branch
finds no slice partition and the pass does what it did.

Tests:
- tests/compile/passes/test_split_coalescing.py as upstream changed it (five
  new test functions beside the one it had). Not run when this patch was exported:
  the cases need a GPU; they are to run on torch 2.13 (the sixth build) and on
  the 2.16 nightly image.

Upstream status: upstream since vllm-project/vllm b39f760c (2026-09-29); drop
this patch when the vLLM base moves past it.
